# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout cannot break the container.
#
# The backend image runs ./scripts/start.sh as its CMD. With core.autocrlf=true
# a Windows clone rewrites shell scripts to CRLF, and COPY bakes them into the
# image, so the shebang becomes "#!/usr/bin/env sh\r" and the container dies
# with "env: 'sh\r': No such file or directory". Linux CI never sees it.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
